@Test
void omitsUserAndPortUnlessTheUserSuppliedThem() {
    var runner = new RecordingRunner(false);
    var installer = installer(runner);
    var archive = ...; manifest = ...;
    var aliasOnly = SshTarget.ofHost("deploy-alias");
    installer.install(aliasOnly, verified(manifest, archive), new RemoteHostInstaller.Platform("linux","x64","/home/tester"));
    List<List<String>> aliasCommands = List.copyOf(runner.commands);
    for (List<String> command : aliasCommands) {
        assertFalse(command.contains("-p"));
        assertFalse(command.contains("-P"));
        assertFalse(command.contains("-i"));
        assertTrue(command.stream().noneMatch(value -> value.contains("@")));   // careful: scripts contain @? 
    }
}
```
Hmm, the ssh script may contain "@"? Unlikely. But the identity store path doesn't. The scripts contain `$HOME`, etc. Let me instead check the destination operand position: for ssh it's `command.get(indexOf("BatchMode=yes")+2)`? Simpler: assert `command.contains("deploy-alias") && !command.contains("user@deploy-alias")`. That's precise.

