Also `java.util.file.Path.of("/data/ssh-known-hosts")` on Windows becomes `\data\ssh-known-hosts` → absolute? `Path.of("/data/ssh-known-hosts").toAbsolutePath()` on Windows → `E:\data\ssh-known-hosts`. Then `UserKnownHostsFile=E:\data\ssh-known-hosts`. My assertion `contains("UserKnownHostsFile=/data/ssh-known-hosts")` would fail on Windows. Use a Windows-safe assertion: `assertTrue(aliasArgs.stream().anyMatch(v -> v.startsWith("UserKnownHostsFile=")))`.

